1
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:13,360
Brighten it up and step back to look.

2
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:26,860
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa.

3
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:33,980
Kick a pebble and even
your shoe goes flying.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,220
And to the carpenter's boss
who had been saving money,

5
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:48,460
I was laughed at for
still acting like a kid.

6
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:53,560
Even if I send some energy somewhere,

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,660
Katsushika Kameari,
another yawn, nothing changes.

8
00:00:58,660 --> 00:01:02,520
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

9
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:10,520
From the pointed-hat water tower,

10
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:16,780
the sunset falls toward the observatory.

11
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow will also end just like this,
won't it.

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,280
Hey, Katsushika Shibamata,
even happiness gets lost.

13
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:34,040
I only realized it because I'm such a fool.

14
00:01:39,460 --> 00:01:41,760
Bonus Battle 3

15
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:45,560
Lingering disfavor

16
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:48,300
Financial institutions keep
collapsing one after another.

17
00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:53,540
Every company across Japan is
suffering from a management crisis.

18
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:58,660
Because sales only rose
during the World Cup.

19
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:01,180
Satellite antennas did sell, though.

20
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:03,520
Ours had nothing to do with it at all.

21
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:06,660
But the reason we're suffering is

22
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:09,380
simply the government's failure to act?

23
00:02:09,380 --> 00:02:12,300
No, the biggest cause is this man.

24
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:16,980
He always takes merchandise on credit,

25
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:19,200
and never once tries to pay back his debts.

26
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:21,700
Yet this man, despite this unpopularity,

27
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:24,100
is about to get his hands on a bonus.

28
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:26,600
Can we stand for this, everyone?

29
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:27,580
Forgive me!

30
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:32,600
This year, I'll tear that bonus right out of this man's hands,
no matter what.

31
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:34,760
Brace yourself, Kankichi Ryotsu!

32
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:35,680
Yeah!

33
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:45,860
Now, we will begin the strategy meeting
for the 25th Ryotsu Kankichi Bonus Battle.

34
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:48,500
Good, good.

35
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:52,000
Kikuchi, did your wife run off on you again?

36
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:55,100
This time, my wife is really serious.

37
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:58,680
If I fail at collecting these debts, then...

38
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,560
If I fail this time too, I'm...

39
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,860
You'll be working for free
to cover Ryo-san's tab.

40
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:06,660
We're all in the same boat.

41
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:10,880
So what kind of new weapons did you prepare this year?
Model kits or something?

42
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:14,800
Last year, it was Operation Peeping Eye.

43
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:17,500
We kept a close watch on Ryo-san's every move,
didn't we?

44
00:03:18,260 --> 00:03:20,420
Before that, it was Ryo-Navi, and then...

45
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,720
Well, the debt collection weapon,
Shakking X.

46
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:28,720
Hey, you've prepared even more new weapons this year than before,
haven't you?

47
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:32,247
Sorry, we couldn't beat today's tide either,

48
00:03:32,297 --> 00:03:36,280
and we didn't have the testing or
the time to develop new weapons.

49
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:37,460
What!?

50
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:39,600
So there are no new weapons this year?

51
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:42,740
I never counted on opportunities
from the start, though.

52
00:03:42,740 --> 00:03:43,142
Ugh,

53
00:03:43,192 --> 00:03:47,420
then how are we supposed to
collect the debt from Ryo-san!?

54
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:50,005
Don't worry. We may have no new weapons,

55
00:03:50,055 --> 00:03:52,340
but I've prepared a foolproof strategy.

56
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:54,340
A strategy?

57
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:59,500
It's called the ABCD Encirclement Net.

58
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:02,120
ABCD Encirclement Net?

59
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:04,500
That's right. These ABCDs will

60
00:04:04,550 --> 00:04:07,980
slowly corner Kankichi Ryotsu.

61
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:10,840
I don't really get it,
but it sounds impressive.

62
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:13,780
Kankichi Ryotsu.

63
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:18,140
This year, take every last yen of his bonus,
I'm begging you.

64
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:24,400
Are you sick, senpai?

65
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:27,220
Shouldn't you go home and rest?

66
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:29,840
Idiot! Tomorrow is bonus day!

67
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:31,720
As soon as I get my bonus,

68
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:36,840
I have to go buy a commercial game console
from the limited-quantity special sale.

69
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:38,100
How could I just sleep through this?

70
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:42,420
I see, the bonus battle season
has come around again this year.

71
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:45,020
There's no bonus battle this year.

72
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:47,860
But the shopping district people...

73
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:51,520
We have a special plan to outwit them.

74
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:54,680
Not a single yen goes to them this year.

75
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:25,260
It's in! It's in!

76
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:29,480
Who'd have thought I'd switch
to bank transfers this year?

77
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:31,640
Even those guys never imagined it.

78
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:35,820
Now, time to withdraw the whole amount.

79
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:37,640
Alright, then.

80
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:41,980
It's me. Maria.

81
00:05:41,980 --> 00:05:44,440
Ryo-sama, today's bonus day, isn't it?

82
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:46,440
Shall we have dinner together?

83
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:48,280
If you're treating, sure.

84
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:51,120
Yes. By the way, Ryo-sama.

85
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:53,640
When will you come to collect your bonus?

86
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:56,620
I've been waiting for you at
the police box for a while now.

87
00:05:57,820 --> 00:06:00,400
Actually,
I switched to bank transfers this year.

88
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:02,980
To outsmart the debt collectors, you see.

89
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:04,980
So where are you now?

90
00:06:05,460 --> 00:06:07,160
At the Suchara Bank in front of the station.

91
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:10,760
Right at this point -

92
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:13,860
What's wrong with you?

93
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:16,640
Eeeeeeh!

94
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:20,780
Aaaaaaah!

95
00:06:20,780 --> 00:06:22,180
Aaaaaaah!

96
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:22,480
Aaaaaaah!

97
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:23,100
Aaaaaaah!

98
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:24,540
Hey, wait!

99
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:30,420
I've been caught!

100
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:34,780
Trying to go after the police officers' bonuses,
you scoundrel!

101
00:06:36,260 --> 00:06:38,640
So I'm under arrest too, right?

102
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,160
Of course.

103
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:41,520
Please.

104
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:44,540
Good, that's the right attitude.

105
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:48,040
Wait, if we arrest him right here and now -

106
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,620
we have to take him to the station.

107
00:06:49,620 --> 00:06:51,060
If we go to the station now -

108
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:53,740
Mass production!

109
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:54,880
Catch him!

110
00:06:56,740 --> 00:06:59,040
That's definitely the loan shark Eijiki!

111
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:02,880
I thought so,
but I'll let you off for today.

112
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:06,960
Why? I was trying to steal money!

113
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:09,420
I'm the victim, and I say it's fine.

114
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:10,200
No way.

115
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:14,160
When something joyous happens,
there's a celebration, right?

116
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:17,620
Today is civil servants' bonus day,
truly a joyous occasion.

117
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:19,540
So it's a congratulatory visit.

118
00:07:21,060 --> 00:07:27,960
No way! Please, arrest me!
What's this? Please, please, please!

119
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:28,380
Please.

120
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:31,220
Stop it.

121
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:35,580
What are you doing?

122
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:38,660
So you're taking me to the
station for questioning now, right?

123
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:40,240
Please, go ahead.

124
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:43,020
You idiot, if we go to the station now,

125
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:46,440
There he is, over there!

126
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:47,480
He's carrying his bonus!

127
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:50,640
Don't move! That bonus is ours now!

128
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:53,220
Why are those guys here?

129
00:07:53,660 --> 00:07:55,740
Please, hurry up and take me in!

130
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,580
This is no time for that!

131
00:07:58,200 --> 00:07:58,920
Prepare yourself!

132
00:07:59,700 --> 00:08:00,220
Damn it!

133
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:02,200
What are you doing?!

134
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:03,160
Yaah!

135
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:08,100
I see, you plan to knock
me out so I can't resist

136
00:08:09,320 --> 00:08:11,460
Using an innocent person
as a shield is cowardly!

137
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:13,100
My bonus is on the line here!

138
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:14,860
I can't afford to care how I look!

139
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:20,960
I won't resist, I promise!

140
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:23,800
Please just take me quietly!

141
00:08:30,020 --> 00:08:31,960
That's not the police station.

142
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:35,160
After him! Chase him!

143
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:45,000
Looks like we lost them.

144
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:47,040
Who were those people just now?

145
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:48,800
It's a bit of a complicated story.

146
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:51,880
Oh no, I forgot to bring the key.

147
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:55,500
Are they maybe underlings of some
yakuza you arrested back in the day?

148
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:58,340
In that case, let's get to the
police station as fast as we can.

149
00:08:58,340 --> 00:09:00,700
They're not police colleagues chasing us,
are they?

150
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:04,940
This guy keeps going on and on about the police,
the police.

151
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:08,980
And him putting the cuffs on
himself seems suspicious, too.

152
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:13,240
Could he be a spy hired
by the debt collectors?

153
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:17,380
With this, we can spy on Ryo-san...

154
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:18,200
Understood.

155
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:22,560
And you report his whereabouts
to us every step of the way.

156
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:27,100
If that's the case,
being with this guy is dangerous.

157
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:28,860
We have to get these handcuffs off quickly.

158
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:31,140
Come here for a second.

159
00:09:31,140 --> 00:09:32,780
So we're going to the police station, right?

160
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:37,020
Not yet?

161
00:09:37,620 --> 00:09:38,600
Hold on a second.

162
00:09:39,380 --> 00:09:40,700
What's going on, Volbo?

163
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:42,460
I need the handcuff key.

164
00:09:42,460 --> 00:09:44,920
It's in the back of my desk drawer.

165
00:09:45,660 --> 00:09:46,940
Got it, Ryotsu.

166
00:09:47,680 --> 00:09:49,620
So where should I take it?

167
00:09:49,620 --> 00:09:52,640
Under the iron bridge
north of Nakagawa Bridge.

168
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,120
Roger.

169
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:05,880
Why do we have to hide in a place like this, Officer?
Just keep quiet.

170
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:12,260
There you are, I've been waiting.
Were you waiting for us all along?

171
00:10:12,260 --> 00:10:15,200
Looks like you're ready to pay your debts.

172
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:17,240
How did you two get here?

173
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:18,700
I knew it, it's you!

174
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:20,180
Attack!

175
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:25,760
How about it?

176
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:27,500
Same tricks won't work on me.

177
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,060
Ryo-san

178
00:10:42,260 --> 00:10:44,880
You're not getting away!

179
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:50,240
Come on, no more back talk.

180
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:52,580
If you're so eager to be arrested,
follow us.

181
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:53,960
Aaaaah!

182
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:03,080
Who'd have thought he'd jump into the river!
No matter how he struggles, he won't get away.

183
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:07,400
My ironclad ABCD Encirclement Net,
and yet...

184
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:12,740
I thought I was going to die.

185
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:18,340
Quit playing dumb already!

186
00:11:19,460 --> 00:11:22,760
I've got a pretty good idea
you're in cahoots with those guys.

187
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:25,420
Didn't you call those guys over earlier?

188
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:27,140
W-what are you talking about?

189
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:28,860
The debt collectors, obviously.

190
00:11:28,860 --> 00:11:31,660
How much do they pay you
to hand me over to them?

191
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:33,580
N-no, that's not it!

192
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:35,220
Then what is it?

193
00:11:35,220 --> 00:11:37,820
I'm being hounded by debt collectors too.

194
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,620
W-what?

195
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:56,120
This is the small company I run.

196
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:57,980
So you're the company president?

197
00:11:59,140 --> 00:12:00,720
Here's the head office.

198
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:03,200
My name is Ichimonji.

199
00:12:04,300 --> 00:12:05,720
It's kind of lifeless here, isn't it.

200
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:08,540
With this recession,
we're on the verge of bankruptcy.

201
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:12,580
I went to the bank to ask for a loan again today,
but they turned me down.

202
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:13,960
So that's how it is.

203
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:17,740
I haven't paid my employees their
salaries for three months now.

204
00:12:18,340 --> 00:12:19,920
I'm a useless man.

205
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:22,760
Why did you think of getting arrested?

206
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:27,300
I thought if I did,
someone else would take over the management.

207
00:12:27,660 --> 00:12:29,600
I'm sure it would go better that way.

208
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:35,400
You know, if the president gets arrested, the
company loses its credibility and usually goes under.

209
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:36,360
I-I see.

210
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:39,220
You should think ahead before you act.

211
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:41,540
And you've been running a company like that?

212
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:44,860
I'm often told I lack foresight.

213
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:45,900
President.

214
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:48,980
No, everyone's doing their best.

215
00:12:48,980 --> 00:12:53,580
Keiko-chan came home early from school a while ago,
saying she felt sick.

216
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:54,600
What?

217
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:57,180
Hey, this Keiko is...

218
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:58,600
my only daughter.

219
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:02,020
She's in third grade, but she's frail.

220
00:13:02,980 --> 00:13:03,900
Wait.

221
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:10,600
I can't let my daughter see
me dressed like this, can I?

222
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:11,840
Sorry.

223
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:14,680
Keiko, are you all right?

224
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:15,740
Dad.

225
00:13:16,260 --> 00:13:17,720
How are you feeling, Keiko?

226
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:20,460
I just felt a little dizzy. I'm fine now.

227
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:22,260
I see.

228
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,820
Dad, who's that man?

229
00:13:24,820 --> 00:13:28,200
That man was going to
fire Dad out of a cannon...

230
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:30,660
W-what?

231
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:33,980
If I tell the truth, there's no point
in hiding the handcuffs, is there?

232
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:35,260
R-right, you're right.

233
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:36,340
Taiho?

234
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:40,040
Yes, yes, we were fellow
members of the Taiho fan club.

235
00:13:40,040 --> 00:13:42,980
Do you know Taiho? That old sumo wrestler.

236
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:45,920
Dad used to like sumo?

237
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:48,660
Even though he says he can't
stand even watching it now.

238
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:52,100
He used to love it, didn't he?

239
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:53,380
W-well...

240
00:13:54,820 --> 00:13:55,700
I-I did love it!

241
00:13:57,460 --> 00:14:00,920
How about some snacks? Hey, snacks.

242
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:01,800
We don't have any.

243
00:14:02,020 --> 00:14:04,230
What? When kids come home from school,

244
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:06,540
they're supposed to have a snack, you know!

245
00:14:07,980 --> 00:14:11,180
We can barely manage daily meals,
let alone snacks.

246
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:15,060
Even when I was a kid,
I got at least a snack.

247
00:14:15,380 --> 00:14:18,832
It's fine. I don't really want to eat right now,
and besides,

248
00:14:18,882 --> 00:14:23,340
they're going to buy me an
amazing Christmas present.

249
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:25,500
Dollhouse set

250
00:14:26,820 --> 00:14:28,040
Are you going to buy that?

251
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:31,840
Yeah, so I'm fine without snacks.

252
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,300
Hey, come here for a sec.

253
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:37,860
Hey, if you get the full set,
that stuff costs tens of thousands!

254
00:14:37,860 --> 00:14:39,640
You're in debt, aren't you?

255
00:14:40,620 --> 00:14:41,560
Yes, but...

256
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:46,180
Wow, a Mika-chan House!

257
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:50,520
Thanks, Mommy, I really wanted this!

258
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:53,180
I bought it because
Yumi-chan has been a good girl.

259
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:57,740
I'll buy it for you this Christmas, Keiko.

260
00:14:57,740 --> 00:14:58,660
Really?

261
00:14:59,200 --> 00:14:59,560
Yeah.

262
00:15:00,380 --> 00:15:04,320
Yay! I wish Christmas
would hurry up and come!

263
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:08,380
You really have no sense of planning. It's that girl who'll be sad later,
you know.

264
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:10,300
I know that, but...

265
00:15:10,300 --> 00:15:15,000
Hey, why have you two been pressed up
against each other like that this whole time?

266
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:18,860
It's the rule of the Taiho Fan Club.

267
00:15:18,860 --> 00:15:22,660
When we meet after a long time, we're supposed
to press our bodies together and wrestle sumo.

268
00:15:25,820 --> 00:15:26,280
Watch out!

269
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:27,160
Watch out!

270
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:28,180
Come on, come on, come on!

271
00:15:31,340 --> 00:15:32,520
You, do you have a wife?

272
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:35,260
Right now, I live with my daughter alone.

273
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:35,960
There you are!

274
00:15:36,460 --> 00:15:38,560
In that case, if you go to prison,

275
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:40,620
Keiko will be left all alone, you know!

276
00:15:40,980 --> 00:15:42,060
I-I see.

277
00:15:42,340 --> 00:15:44,940
Think a little about the future before you act,
will you?

278
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:47,900
If some relative takes in your daughter,

279
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:49,320
that's what I was thinking.

280
00:15:49,980 --> 00:15:51,640
Everyone's having a hard time these days,
you know.

281
00:15:51,860 --> 00:15:53,800
Do you have any relatives
who would take her in?

282
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:57,300
Besides, children are best
off living with their parents.

283
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:00,120
Don't you ever think about
getting arrested again.

284
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:01,000
Got it?

285
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:01,700
Yes.

286
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:03,200
I won't do it again.

287
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:06,680
Alright, then the remaining problem is this.

288
00:16:07,860 --> 00:16:10,720
They've probably already spread
the word to the station too,

289
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:11,740
so what do we do?

290
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:14,340
I've got a good idea.

291
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:22,580
My family's motorbike shop?

292
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:27,600
If we use the tools there,
we can at least get those handcuffs off.

293
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:29,920
Understood. I'll go pick them up right away.

294
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:42,500
Here they come.

295
00:16:42,840 --> 00:16:44,080
Honda, it's here!

296
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:50,360
Hey, mister,
isn't it about time you paid up?

297
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:52,460
You've got to pay back what you borrowed.

298
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:55,200
Hurry up and load the bike!

299
00:16:55,580 --> 00:16:57,260
We can't fit any more than three riders!

300
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:59,000
Are you planning to betray us?

301
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,580
I'm saying this for your sake!

302
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:05,160
This is your chance to go straight!

303
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:06,040
Damn it!

304
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:09,460
That's right! Go straight, Ryotsu!

305
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:12,620
You betrayed us like this, you bastard!

306
00:17:13,760 --> 00:17:17,120
Ryo-sama! Please stop piling up more crimes!

307
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:19,260
Brutus, you too?

308
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:36,040
It seems the time has finally come for you to give up,
Ryo-san.

309
00:17:38,820 --> 00:17:42,240
So Maria and the others
told them where I was

310
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:44,960
Today's bonus day, right?

311
00:17:45,860 --> 00:17:46,840
Got it.

312
00:17:46,840 --> 00:17:49,360
Understood, I'll pick you up right away.

313
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:55,280
That's right. I've learned the terror of the ABCD encirclement,
Ryo-san.

314
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:57,400
ABCD encirclement, you say?

315
00:17:57,720 --> 00:18:00,380
A stands for the A of Asatobai.

316
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,340
I'm sorry, Lord Ryo.

317
00:18:02,780 --> 00:18:05,700
But this is your chance, Lord Ryo,
to become a true human being.

318
00:18:06,060 --> 00:18:09,300
To have a clean body free of germs,
and with me...

319
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:10,920
No way, I'm not doing that.

320
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:14,660
B stands for the B of Volvo Saigo.

321
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:17,860
I'm working for the shopping district folks.

322
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:20,700
That's why I'll give it my all!

323
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:24,700
And D is Honda's Dano...

324
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:27,020
It's D.

325
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:28,620
That's quite a stretch, isn't it.

326
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:33,960
Besides, Volvo starts with a V! Not a B!

327
00:18:34,900 --> 00:18:36,540
Don't sweat the small stuff!

328
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:39,500
Wait. Then who's going to be C?

329
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:42,420
So we need a name with a C...

330
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:43,680
A name with "ji" attached, then.

331
00:18:43,680 --> 00:18:47,880
Hey, Terai, Nakagawa, go!

332
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:50,640
Ohara: Nope, that's wrong.

333
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:58,540
Don't tell me it's you...
No, that's not right. The C is this man.

334
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:07,000
Keep them waiting, will you? Ugh, where's a
"c" supposed to go in this guy's name?

335
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:10,920
Flip Matsunosuke's corner lot upside down,
and it becomes "ii."

336
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:12,440
That's ridiculous.

337
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:15,880
I'm going to knock some sense
into you while I have the chance.

338
00:19:16,420 --> 00:19:17,880
I'm doing this for your sake too.

339
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:23,440
Then all these non-retail Docu-Memo goods will be yours,
Sakonji.

340
00:19:23,800 --> 00:19:24,160
Thank you very much.

341
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:26,860
So you got bought off, didn't you?

342
00:19:28,020 --> 00:19:29,520
You guys got a little something too, right?

343
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:32,740
Well, I didn't get any
model guns or anything.

344
00:19:32,740 --> 00:19:37,120
And a year's worth of shoujo manga,
or pair tickets to an amusement park...

345
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:40,380
...or invitations to a luxury spa.

346
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:41,380
Just as I thought.

347
00:19:41,380 --> 00:19:44,600
Ryotsu, you of all people should understand.

348
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:48,500
As a fan,
I can't let this opportunity slip away.

349
00:19:48,500 --> 00:19:51,040
Hey, Saorin!

350
00:19:57,380 --> 00:20:27,200
Hyped, hyped, hyped, hyped,
hyped, hyped, hyped, hyped...

351
00:20:28,540 --> 00:20:30,480
This girl is frail.

352
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:31,940
Don't make a racket.

353
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:34,080
Well, my apologies.

354
00:20:35,540 --> 00:20:37,060
I didn't come here to talk about that.

355
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:38,120
Just hear me out.

356
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:40,640
That girl is this guy's daughter, though.

357
00:20:40,640 --> 00:20:43,120
The more I hear,
the more pitiful their family situation is.

358
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:46,300
With this recession,
his company is struggling financially.

359
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:49,880
The employees haven't been
paid their salaries in months.

360
00:20:50,380 --> 00:20:52,180
Even daily life is a struggle.

361
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:56,220
My wife died a few years ago,
leaving behind high

362
00:20:57,380 --> 00:21:00,540
My daughter is sickly,
but I can't even afford her medicine.

363
00:21:00,540 --> 00:21:02,900
What a pitiful story.

364
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:08,620
Driven to despair,
this man even tried to turn to crime.

365
00:21:10,420 --> 00:21:11,220
Is that true?

366
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:13,260
More or less.

367
00:21:13,820 --> 00:21:17,980
Is there anyone among you
more unfortunate than this man?

368
00:21:19,460 --> 00:21:21,020
That's when I made up my mind.

369
00:21:21,020 --> 00:21:24,040
Rather than let you take this bonus,

370
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:26,640
I'll donate all of it to this man.

371
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,120
Are you sure about this?

372
00:21:30,120 --> 00:21:31,800
A man never goes back on his word.

373
00:21:31,800 --> 00:21:35,100
Take good care of it.
Really, really good care.

374
00:21:35,740 --> 00:21:36,140
Yes.

375
00:21:36,140 --> 00:21:37,940
You understand, right?

376
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:40,180
Of course I understand.

377
00:21:40,180 --> 00:21:41,540
Lord Ryo.

378
00:21:42,840 --> 00:21:44,180
Just as expected of you, Lord Ryo.

379
00:21:44,180 --> 00:21:46,700
No wonder I fell for you.

380
00:21:46,700 --> 00:21:48,280
Ryotsu, I've got a new respect for you.

381
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:51,580
I'm pathetic for being
bought off with a toy gun.

382
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:54,100
I'll go get the handcuff key.

383
00:21:54,860 --> 00:21:56,820
Lend a helping hand to the weak.

384
00:21:59,380 --> 00:22:01,660
Yo! Ryotsu-ya!
You're a real Edokko, aren't you!

385
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:08,380
Senpai, I heard about it.

386
00:22:09,020 --> 00:22:09,990
He gave away his entire bonus,

387
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:13,100
to the owner of a small factory on the verge of bankruptcy,
apparently.

388
00:22:13,780 --> 00:22:16,460
That's amazing.
Most people couldn't do that.

389
00:22:16,920 --> 00:22:20,000
As if I'd ever hand my
bonus over to someone else.

390
00:22:20,460 --> 00:22:21,300
You fool.

391
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:22,900
But...

392
00:22:22,900 --> 00:22:26,560
I only temporarily stashed it
there to dodge the loan sharks' eyes.

393
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:29,040
He knows that too.

394
00:22:29,040 --> 00:22:31,140
I'm going to collect it now.

395
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:34,020
I thought as much.

396
00:22:36,980 --> 00:22:37,780
Yes.

397
00:22:38,720 --> 00:22:39,480
Ryo-san

398
00:22:40,060 --> 00:22:42,020
Thank you so much for yesterday.

399
00:22:43,120 --> 00:22:44,340
Thank you?
That's not what you should be saying.

400
00:22:44,340 --> 00:22:45,020
Here.

401
00:22:46,220 --> 00:22:46,620
Yeah.

402
00:22:48,460 --> 00:22:49,900
Thank you so much.

403
00:22:50,700 --> 00:22:51,960
I didn't come here to be applauded.

404
00:22:51,960 --> 00:22:53,880
It's the bonus I gave you yesterday.

405
00:22:53,880 --> 00:22:55,840
You said you understood, didn't you?

406
00:22:56,560 --> 00:23:00,180
Yes, of course.
I fully understand what Mr. Ryotsu has done.

407
00:23:00,540 --> 00:23:03,960
The bonus you gave me went toward
employees' salaries and the company's debts,

408
00:23:04,300 --> 00:23:08,240
and also toward a Christmas
present for my daughter.

409
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:14,500
S-so, don't tell me my bonus was...

410
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:14,832
Yes.

411
00:23:14,882 --> 00:23:18,580
Not a single yen of
Ryotsu's kindness was wasted.

412
00:23:18,900 --> 00:23:20,880
We used every bit of it.

413
00:23:22,500 --> 00:23:25,820
When I said I understood,
I didn't mean it like that...

414
00:23:27,560 --> 00:23:27,840
Mister!

415
00:23:29,140 --> 00:23:31,320
Keiko was overjoyed last night.

416
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:34,620
Thanks to Ryotsu,
we were able to get the Mika-chan House.

417
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:37,280
No, that's, well...

418
00:23:37,620 --> 00:23:39,680
Here! This is a present!

419
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:41,660
T-this is...

420
00:23:44,520 --> 00:23:48,400
My daughter drew it with all her heart.
Please accept it.

421
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:52,840
So this drawing is all I
get for my bonus this year?

422
00:23:53,780 --> 00:23:55,320
Mister, let's play together!

423
00:23:55,320 --> 00:23:57,760
No, I'm playing house with the dolls...

424
00:24:15,480 --> 00:24:17,780
With surprise and commotion,

425
00:24:18,320 --> 00:24:20,680
untangling together, and solving it,

426
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:23,700
swift and sharp, cutting away,

427
00:24:36,440 --> 00:24:40,060
more than anything, an incredible power.

428
00:24:40,060 --> 00:24:46,100
Gather everyone, come here,

429
00:24:46,940 --> 00:24:52,360
like a dream, the final energy.

430
00:24:53,360 --> 00:24:56,780
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday,

431
00:24:56,780 --> 00:24:59,700
drawing the universe,
standing on the ground.

432
00:24:59,700 --> 00:25:03,420
The star of Kameari is coming,
and the reason is strange.

433
00:25:03,420 --> 00:25:04,580
Aaaaah!

434
00:25:05,960 --> 00:25:07,140
This should be fine, right?

435
00:25:07,140 --> 00:25:08,640
Like hell it is!

436
00:25:22,240 --> 00:25:24,780
Damn that old man Ohara!

437
00:25:24,780 --> 00:25:28,260
Sure, he's married, but the
bastard's getting all cozy with Keiko!

438
00:25:28,260 --> 00:25:29,660
This is so infuriating!

439
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:32,580
If it comes to this,
with Ryotsu-style substitution jutsu,

440
00:25:33,420 --> 00:25:34,120
I'll play a prank on him!

441
00:25:34,640 --> 00:25:36,600
Next time: Bookshelf Substitute Sword!

442
00:25:37,080 --> 00:25:37,580
See you!

